-- mod-hearthstone: the class deck hint of the Hearthstone Masters. Once the whole introduction (Byron's trade, quest 5)
-- is turned in, Ezra Chatterton (919501) and Ibelin Redmoore (919502) answer "Where can I learn to play other class
-- decks?" (src/HsIntroGlue.cpp, kClassHints). The answer is a class list, and every class has its own reply that
-- tells a story and names the teacher and the place:
--   9195150 Ezra's class list, 9195700-9195708 his replies (Horde teachers)
--   9195151 Ibelin's class list, 9195710-9195718 his replies (Alliance teachers)
-- Reply order: Warrior, Paladin, Hunter, Rogue, Priest, Shaman, Mage, Warlock, Druid (the order of the deck items).
-- The texts are mirrored in the class hint doc. Rebuilt each run. No backslashes, no semicolons in strings.

DELETE FROM `npc_text` WHERE `ID` IN (9195150, 9195151, 9195700, 9195701, 9195702, 9195703, 9195704, 9195705, 9195706, 9195707, 9195708, 9195710, 9195711, 9195712, 9195713, 9195714, 9195715, 9195716, 9195717, 9195718);
DELETE FROM `broadcast_text` WHERE `entry` IN (9195150, 9195151, 9195700, 9195701, 9195702, 9195703, 9195704, 9195705, 9195706, 9195707, 9195708, 9195710, 9195711, 9195712, 9195713, 9195714, 9195715, 9195716, 9195717, 9195718);

INSERT INTO `broadcast_text` (`entry`, `male_text`, `female_text`) VALUES
  (9195150,
   'Other class decks?$B$BI wish I had a stack of them to hand out, $N. I do not. Every deck I ever owned is already on a table somewhere, in somebody else''s hands.$B$BBut this game has spread further than you would think. Players have settled in all our cities now, each with a style of their own. Most of them will not bother with a beginner, so come to them at level ten or higher.$B$BWhich style are you curious about? I will tell you what I know, and who to ask.',
   'Other class decks?$B$BI wish I had a stack of them to hand out, $N. I do not. Every deck I ever owned is already on a table somewhere, in somebody else''s hands.$B$BBut this game has spread further than you would think. Players have settled in all our cities now, each with a style of their own. Most of them will not bother with a beginner, so come to them at level ten or higher.$B$BWhich style are you curious about? I will tell you what I know, and who to ask.'),
  (9195151,
   'Other class decks?$B$BI am afraid I cannot help you there, $N. I do not have a spare deck to my name. Everything I had went to students who needed it more.$B$BBut the game has found its way into every corner of the Alliance. Players have taken their seats in the cities, each one devoted to a single style. Most of them will not bother with a beginner, so come to them at level ten or higher.$B$BWhich style are you curious about? I will tell you what I know, and who to ask.',
   'Other class decks?$B$BI am afraid I cannot help you there, $N. I do not have a spare deck to my name. Everything I had went to students who needed it more.$B$BBut the game has found its way into every corner of the Alliance. Players have taken their seats in the cities, each one devoted to a single style. Most of them will not bother with a beginner, so come to them at level ten or higher.$B$BWhich style are you curious about? I will tell you what I know, and who to ask.'),
  (9195700,
   'Warrior?$B$BThat one is easy. Here in Orgrimmar there is an old soldier named Zerok. Veteran of three wars. He plays warrior. Always warrior. I have never once seen him touch another class.$B$BYou will find him in the Valley of Strength.$B$BBut be aware, he is not a patient teacher, but he knows his deck better than anyone.',
   'Warrior?$B$BThat one is easy. Here in Orgrimmar there is an old soldier named Zerok. Veteran of three wars. He plays warrior. Always warrior. I have never once seen him touch another class.$B$BYou will find him in the Valley of Strength.$B$BBut be aware, he is not a patient teacher, but he knows his deck better than anyone.'),
  (9195701,
   'Paladin?$B$BNow that is a strange request for one of ours. The knights of the Light are not our people, and nobody I know plays them.$B$B...Except one. In the Undercity there is a Forsaken scholar named Drin Lia.I don''t know her well, I just heard stories of others telling me that she is... special. Maybe talk to her. Somewhere in the Apothecarium, I would say.',
   'Paladin?$B$BNow that is a strange request for one of ours. The knights of the Light are not our people, and nobody I know plays them.$B$B...Except one. In the Undercity there is a Forsaken scholar named Drin Lia.I don''t know her well, I just heard stories of others telling me that she is... special. Maybe talk to her. Somewhere in the Apothecarium, I would say.'),
  (9195702,
   'Hunter?$B$BThat would be Boro Softstep, a friend of mine on Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff. A tauren, solemn and unhurried, and very fond of the sound of his own knowledge.',
   'Hunter?$B$BThat would be Boro Softstep, a friend of mine on Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff. A tauren, solemn and unhurried, and very fond of the sound of his own knowledge.'),
  (9195703,
   'Rogue?$B$BNo honest rogue gives lessons, $N. But in the Cleft of Shadow there is a troll called For''sen who deals cards the way he deals everything else. Quietly, and at a small profit.$B$BI hear a deck has gone missing down there, and that everyone you ask tells a different story about who has it.$B$BKeep one hand on your purse. If you want to learn his style, you will have to find the truth yourself.',
   'Rogue?$B$BNo honest rogue gives lessons, $N. But in the Cleft of Shadow there is a troll called For''sen who deals cards the way he deals everything else. Quietly, and at a small profit.$B$BI hear a deck has gone missing down there, and that everyone you ask tells a different story about who has it.$B$BKeep one hand on your purse. If you want to learn his style, you will have to find the truth yourself.'),
  (9195704,
   'Priest?$B$BDown in the Undercity you will find a Forsaken priest named Jeffrey Shih. He spends his days among what old Lordaeron left behind. Broken holy tablets, cards nobody wanted, things the living have thrown away.$B$BHe says it all comes down to perspective. I have never quite followed him. But he plays priest, and he will gladly share what he knows.',
   'Priest?$B$BDown in the Undercity you will find a Forsaken priest named Jeffrey Shih. He spends his days among what old Lordaeron left behind. Broken holy tablets, cards nobody wanted, things the living have thrown away.$B$BHe says it all comes down to perspective. I have never quite followed him. But he plays priest, and he will gladly share what he knows.'),
  (9195705,
   'Shaman?$B$BTo be honest, I have not heard of a Hearthstone teacher for shaman. Not a proper one.$B$BBut on Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff, where the elders teach the old ways, there is a young tauren named Annie Foxstalker. She is always lingering at the edge of the lessons, wanting to become a shaman and not quite daring to ask. I hear she is curious about the game too.$B$BGo and find her. Be gentle, she is shy. Perhaps the two of you can learn together.',
   'Shaman?$B$BTo be honest, I have not heard of a Hearthstone teacher for shaman. Not a proper one.$B$BBut on Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff, where the elders teach the old ways, there is a young tauren named Annie Foxstalker. She is always lingering at the edge of the lessons, wanting to become a shaman and not quite daring to ask. I hear she is curious about the game too.$B$BGo and find her. Be gentle, she is shy. Perhaps the two of you can learn together.'),
  (9195706,
   'Mage?$B$BIn the Undercity there is a Forsaken researcher named Marie Cu Rie. She is a mage, a scientist, and she studies cards the way other people study plague.$B$BShe has a number for every experiment and a note for every result. Do not touch anything on her table unless she asks you to.$B$BIf you can bear being a test subject, nobody knows the arcane side of this game better. I would guess you can find her in the mage quarter.',
   'Mage?$B$BIn the Undercity there is a Forsaken researcher named Marie Cu Rie. She is a mage, a scientist, and she studies cards the way other people study plague.$B$BShe has a number for every experiment and a note for every result. Do not touch anything on her table unless she asks you to.$B$BIf you can bear being a test subject, nobody knows the arcane side of this game better. I would guess you can find her in the mage quarter.'),
  (9195707,
   'Warlock?$B$BIn the Cleft of Shadow, an orc named Varka Ashhand teaches the game to new players.. She plays warlock, she does not smile, and she never wastes a word.$B$BHer imp, Skrit, runs her errands. He will offer you a very good price for everything.$B$BPower has a price, she says. She is usually right. Talk to her.',
   'Warlock?$B$BIn the Cleft of Shadow, an orc named Varka Ashhand teaches the game to new players.. She plays warlock, she does not smile, and she never wastes a word.$B$BHer imp, Skrit, runs her errands. He will offer you a very good price for everything.$B$BPower has a price, she says. She is usually right. Talk to her.'),
  (9195708,
   'Druid?$B$BKolento Treewatcher, on Elder Rise above Mulgore. A tauren, calm as the wind, and the only druid I know who plays this game.$B$BYou want to learn from him, trust me.$B$BAnd bring some patience.',
   'Druid?$B$BKolento Treewatcher, on Elder Rise above Mulgore. A tauren, calm as the wind, and the only druid I know who plays this game.$B$BYou want to learn from him, trust me.$B$BAnd bring some patience.'),
  (9195710,
   'Warrior?$B$BIn Ironforge you will find Steeg Haskell. A dwarf, a veteran, and quite possibly the most serious Hearthstone player I have ever met. He treats every game as a military campaign, and he plays warrior. Only warrior.$B$BThe Deeprun Tram will take you there, he is always in the inn. He will not hand you a deck for nothing, but he may teach you something if you can show him you are worth the lesson.',
   'Warrior?$B$BIn Ironforge you will find Steeg Haskell. A dwarf, a veteran, and quite possibly the most serious Hearthstone player I have ever met. He treats every game as a military campaign, and he plays warrior. Only warrior.$B$BThe Deeprun Tram will take you there, he is always in the inn. He will not hand you a deck for nothing, but he may teach you something if you can show him you are worth the lesson.'),
  (9195711,
   'Paladin?$B$BYou need not even leave the city for this one. In Cathedral Square stands a knight named Sir Rowan Vale, with his squire, Tess. He is modest to a fault.$B$BHe will be the paladin teacher you can find on Azeroth.',
   'Paladin?$B$BYou need not even leave the city for this one. In Cathedral Square stands a knight named Sir Rowan Vale, with his squire, Tess. He is modest to a fault.$B$BHe will be the paladin teacher you can find on Azeroth.'),
  (9195712,
   'Hunter?$B$BAcross the sea in Darnassus, inside the Cenarion Enclave, there is a gnome named Fenn Coilwhistle. Yes, a gnome. He is a hunter, an enthusiastic presenter of wildlife, and a man with an excuse for everything.$B$BPerhaps he can teach you.',
   'Hunter?$B$BAcross the sea in Darnassus, inside the Cenarion Enclave, there is a gnome named Fenn Coilwhistle. Yes, a gnome. He is a hunter, an enthusiastic presenter of wildlife, and a man with an excuse for everything.$B$BPerhaps he can teach you.'),
  (9195713,
   'Rogue?$B$BI will say only this. In Old Town, not far from this tavern, there is a man of the SI:7 named Matt Dixon. Ask him!',
   'Rogue?$B$BI will say only this. In Old Town, not far from this tavern, there is a man of the SI:7 named Matt Dixon. Ask him!'),
  (9195714,
   'Priest?$B$BPriestess Alenya Moonbrook serves in the Temple of the Moon, in Darnassus.$B$BShe once loved this game, and I believe she would be glad of someone to play with.',
   'Priest?$B$BPriestess Alenya Moonbrook serves in the Temple of the Moon, in Darnassus.$B$BShe once loved this game, and I believe she would be glad of someone to play with.'),
  (9195715,
   'Shaman?$B$BThere is a dwarf in Ironforge named John Maloneybrew. A tinkerer, and a loud one. He has been running experiments with totems, and he insists that the right stories and the right battle reports can be built into the perfect shaman. He calls it applied shamanism.$B$BStand well back, and mind the bellows. But if anyone in Ironforge can show you how a shaman plays, it is John.',
   'Shaman?$B$BThere is a dwarf in Ironforge named John Maloneybrew. A tinkerer, and a loud one. He has been running experiments with totems, and he insists that the right stories and the right battle reports can be built into the perfect shaman. He calls it applied shamanism.$B$BStand well back, and mind the bellows. But if anyone in Ironforge can show you how a shaman plays, it is John.'),
  (9195716,
   'Mage?$B$BA human mage named Mitchell Jones. Currently in Darnassus I think. His father copies old histories here in Stormwind, and Mitchell has gone there to collect firsthand accounts of how ordinary people live. Dates and battles, he knows by heart.',
   'Mage?$B$BA human mage named Mitchell Jones. Currently in Darnassus I think. His father copies old histories here in Stormwind, and Mitchell has gone there to collect firsthand accounts of how ordinary people live. Dates and battles, he knows by heart.'),
  (9195717,
   'Warlock?$B$BIn the cellar of the Slaughtered Lamb, here in Stormwind, a woman named Maren Blackquill teaches this style. Downstairs, mind you. Upstairs it is only a tavern.',
   'Warlock?$B$BIn the cellar of the Slaughtered Lamb, here in Stormwind, a woman named Maren Blackquill teaches this style. Downstairs, mind you. Upstairs it is only a tavern.'),
  (9195718,
   'Druid?$B$BThijs Nightbloom, in the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus. A druid, and the most patient person I have ever met.$B$BDo not go to him in a hurry. He will notice, and he will make you wait.',
   'Druid?$B$BThijs Nightbloom, in the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus. A druid, and the most patient person I have ever met.$B$BDo not go to him in a hurry. He will notice, and he will make you wait.');

